-- A cavern, wider and taller than any of the target screens, so it scrolls
-- in both directions.
--
-- The legend names each character, and those names are what Demotic rules
-- collide with — which is why `when player touches spikes` reads as a
-- sentence rather than as an index into a tile table.
--
-- `wall` and `ledge` are both solid and the split is not decorative: the game
-- grounds a jump on a `ledge` and merely stops at a `wall`, so the floor and the
-- platforms are ledges and the shaft's sides and roof are walls. One legend
-- character is the difference between landing on the ground and being able to
-- climb the side of the cave.

tile #  wall    solid  rockwall.svg
tile =  ledge   solid  stone.svg
tile ^  spikes         spikes.svg
tile *  exit           exit.svg
tile .  air            air.svg

map
